# Keep every text file LF in the working tree, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# Several tests assert on the source of a route by matching a few lines of it,
# newline included. With autocrlf on, a branch checkout rewrites those files as
# CRLF, the literal \n in the pattern stops matching, and the suite reports a
# failure in code nobody has touched - which is worse than no test, because it
# is believed for about ten minutes. The files are stored LF either way, so
# this changes nothing about what is committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The modpack is a zip. Normalising it would corrupt it.
*.mrpack binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff2 binary
